# Demo: the Treechat app on a real phone (AWS Device Farm, metered). Same
# read-only walk as demo-treechat.jevb: types a username into sign-up but
# never submits.
#   jevb run examples/demo-treechat-app.jevb --device "pixel 9" --app treechat.apk
#   jevb run examples/demo-treechat-app.jevb --device "iphone 14" --app treechat.ipa
pace human
open
act? dismiss the notifications permission prompt without allowing
check is this a login page?
check is there a password field?
refute is the user already logged in?
act go to create a new account
check is a sign-up form with Username and Email fields shown?   # iOS: the keyboard covers the rest
refute is an error or "not found" page shown?
type the username field => jevb demo
check does the username field contain "jevb demo"?
refute is the password field filled in?
press HideKeyboard       # it covers the sign-up form's Login link
scroll end
act tap Login to go back to the login page
check is a login form with Email and Password fields shown?
refute is an error or "not found" page shown?
